---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import data from '../data/filings.json';
---
<Layout title="ETF Registration Filings: Source-Linked EDGAR Desk Guide" description="Inspect a dated SEC EDGAR search snapshot for ETF registration documents and amendments. Follow original filing links without treating filings as fund launches."><script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Dataset',name:'Partial historical ETF registration search snapshot',description:'Primary documents retained from the first SEC search batch; not an exhaustive feed or verified fund-launch list.',dateModified:data.asOf,temporalCoverage:'2026-10-01/2026-10-16',url:'https://etfnewsdaily.online/filings/',isBasedOn:data.sourceUrl,creator:{'@type':'Organization',name:'SEC EDGAR'}})}/><h1>Registration, not recommendation.</h1><p class="lead">These are ETF-keyword search matches in selected registration forms. A filing does not establish a new fund, SEC approval, an effective date or a trading launch.</p><p class="note">Snapshot observed {data.asOf}. Search window: October 1–16, 2026. Source: <a href={data.sourceUrl}>{data.source}</a>.</p><p>The source returned {data.totalDocuments} document matches. This view keeps primary documents from the first result batch, removes duplicate accession numbers, and excludes exhibits. It is a partial research queue, not an exhaustive newest-first feed.</p><p class="note" id="filing-scroll-help">On a narrow screen, scroll the table horizontally to reach the SEC source links. Keyboard users can focus the table and use arrow keys.</p><div class="scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Historical SEC filing search results" aria-describedby="filing-scroll-help"><table><thead><tr><th>Filed</th><th>Registrant</th><th>Form / document</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.rows.map(r=><tr><td>{r.date}</td><td>{r.filer}</td><td>{r.form}<br/>{r.name}</td><td><a href={r.url}>SEC filing index</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>No launch name is inferred from a registrant’s name. Read the primary prospectus and effective-date language before identifying a product.</p><a href="/methodology/">Coverage and refresh policy</a><p><a href="/guides/">Read ETF field guides</a></p></Layout>